From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:51:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: vdpu381-vp9: reset the register set for every
 frame

The VDPU381 VP9 backend keeps its register set in the codec context and
fills it field by field in config_registers(), but never clears it, so
values from earlier frames leak into later ones:

- The loop filter ref and mode deltas of the previous frame are OR-ed
  into reg94 and reg75, so after a frame that changes the deltas the
  hardware gets the bitwise OR of the old and new values. On
  vp90-2-09-lf_deltas.webm the deltas change from {1, 0, -1, -1} / {0, 0}
  to {2, 0, -2, -2} / {-2, 2} on frame 3, and every frame from the next
  one using the deltas is decoded with the wrong filter strength.

- The per-segment feature enables in reg67-74 are only ever set, so a
  feature stays enabled for a segment after the stream disables it.

Clear the register set before programming each frame, as the H.264 and
HEVC VDPU381 backends already do.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 .../media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c    | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c
index 9b08e32fb..aee9de9a1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu381-vp9.c
@@ -467,6 +467,13 @@ static void config_registers(struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx,
 			(V4L2_VP9_FRAME_FLAG_KEY_FRAME |
 			 V4L2_VP9_FRAME_FLAG_INTRA_ONLY));
 
+	/*
+	 * The register set is kept in the context and only partially written
+	 * below: start from a clean set so that nothing leaks from the
+	 * previous frame.
+	 */
+	memset(regs, 0, sizeof(*regs));
+
 	regs->common.reg009_dec_mode.dec_mode = VDPU381_MODE_VP9;
 
 	regs->vp9_param.reg103.vp9_intra_only_flag = intra_only;
